INT. LUNAR GREENHOUSE DOME - DAY

Rows of tomato plants under pale artificial light. A quiet hum.

ENGINEER ILSE VOGEL (30s, coveralls) prunes a vine. BOTANIST KWAME ASANTE (40s) logs readings on a tablet. They work in comfortable silence.

TECHNICIAN BRONWYN FALK (20s) hauls a crate of seedlings through the airlock, whistling.

KWAME
Good yield this month.

ILSE
Best since the landing.

BRONWYN
Cafeteria will be thrilled.

A comm panel clicks.

COMMANDER (V.O.)
Dome Two, status check.

KWAME
All green, Commander.

COMMANDER (V.O.)
Good. Keep it that way.

The panel clicks off. Ilse snips another stem.

Then the lights flicker. Once. Twice. The hum drops in pitch.

BRONWYN
Was that supposed to happen?

ILSE
No.

Every plant in the row leans toward the airlock door. Slowly. As if something outside were calling them.

KWAME
Everyone stay very still.
